---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-14/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-14/interactions.json';
import {poses} from '../../../../lib/equipment/15-14/solver.mjs';
const a='/equipment/15-14/';
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(typeof v==='object'?JSON.stringify(v):String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Retinal prosthesis bench | Inert concept and dry gauge" subtitle="" description="Inspect an original unbuilt cabinet concept, then use an independent dry geometric clearance gauge." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="dry"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-14/">← Equipment 15-14</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#dry-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">15-14 / Original unbuilt enclosure / Detached geometry exhibit</p><h2>RETINAL PROSTHESIS BENCH CONCEPT</h2><p>The modeled cabinet is an inert, unbuilt concept. On a separate table, check whether a circular puck sits inside a rectangular opening, just touches it, or crosses one or more edges.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the cabinet and gauge</h3><div id="dry-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Case','Gauge','Keys'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button type="button" id="dry-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="dry-model" aria-label="Orbitable inert cabinet concept with an independent metric dry gauge and three position keys"></canvas><p id="dry-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">The separate gauge keys select centered (gray), tangent (teal), or overrun (gold). Click the puck to reread the current pose. No cabinet surface responds.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Read signed clearance</h3><div class="e-fields"><label>Stored puck position<select id="dry-pose">{Object.entries(poses).map(([k,v])=><option value={k} selected={k==='center'}>{v.label}</option>)}</select></label></div><div class="e-row"><button type="button" id="dry-reset">Restore center</button><button type="button" id="dry-json" class="e-run" disabled>Export gauge JSON</button></div><p id="dry-status" role="status">Puck is fully inside</p><p><span id="dry-position">Center: X 0 mm, Z 0 mm</span> · <b>Tightest edge: <span id="dry-minimum">+22 mm</span></b></p>
<svg id="dry-chart" viewBox="0 0 346 217" role="img" aria-label="Plan of a circular puck inside or across a rectangular opening"><rect x="71" y="37" width="198" height="138" fill="#96b0ac" rx="4"/><rect x="80" y="46" width="180" height="120" fill="#e6e6d9" stroke="#385a64" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M65 106h240M170 30v160" fill="none" stroke="#879798" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/><circle id="dry-disk" cx="170" cy="106" r="27" class="clear"/><text x="267" y="98" fill="#385766" font-size="13">+X</text><text x="174" y="187" fill="#385766" font-size="13">+Z</text><text x="39" y="207" fill="#385766" font-size="12">Equal X/Z scale (mm) · operator faces +Z</text></svg>
<div class="e-over"><table><caption>Clearance from puck to opening edge</caption><thead><tr><th>Left</th><th>Right</th><th>Rear</th><th>Front</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td id="dry-left">+42 mm</td><td id="dry-right">+42 mm</td><td id="dry-rear">+22 mm</td><td id="dry-front">+22 mm</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section></div>
<section id="dry-references"><h3>Original geometry and limits</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original gray cabinet with a separate dry gauge on a second table"/><figcaption>Original cabinet concept and separate dry-gauge table. No commercial product, and no manufactured or measured prototype, is claimed.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original technical overview of aperture rails and round puck"/><figcaption>The opening and puck dimensions are authored reference values. The three stored center offsets change the displayed puck position and readout together.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Assembly</th><th>Original authored dimensions</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Concept cabinet W × D × H</td><td>420 × 340 × 232 mm</td><td>Digital glTF bounds including feet; not measured hardware.</td></tr><tr><td>Detached gauge clear opening</td><td>120 × 80 mm</td><td>X width, Z depth. Dimensions checked against the four authored meshes.</td></tr><tr><td>Detached puck</td><td>36 mm diameter</td><td>Circular geometry at the four computed edge limits.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Each clearance is the normal distance from the puck center to an edge minus the puck radius. Positive means clear, zero is tangent, and negative means overrun. This is only a dry two-dimensional clearance calculation with no contact force or tolerance stack-up. No biological specimen, light, electricity, implants, stimulation, treatment, fabrication, or working hardware is included. The original register’s physical acceptance is outside this scope.</p></section>
<section id="dry-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{show(x.expected)}</td><td>{show(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'example-gauge.json'}>Example JSON</a> · <a href={a+'concept-cabinet-dry-gauge.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} draw primitives. Optional WebXR; headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-14/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#dry header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#dry h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#dry section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#dry button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#dry button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#dry-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#dry .e-fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}#dry select{min-height:2.45rem;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border)}#dry-chart{display:block;width:min(100%,450px);height:auto;background:#ede9de}#dry-disk{stroke:#2f5360;stroke-width:2.5;fill-opacity:.72}#dry-disk.clear{fill:#b58b3c}#dry-disk.touching{fill:#6594ad}#dry-disk.outside{fill:#c67151;stroke:#7d392c}#dry table caption{caption-side:top;font-size:.81rem}</style>


